WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.770
Though he may not be at his most recognizable
in his role in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.900
2, the actor who plays Tullk in the Marvel
sequel is bound to look familiar to any avid

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:10.900
moviegoer.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.419
His name is Tommy Flanagan, an actor with
a mile-long resume and a pair of distinctive

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:16.419
scars.

00:00:16.419 --> 00:00:19.170
He's one of those actors whose name you can't
quite remember, but whose face you know by

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.170
heart.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.779
Here are a few flicks you might have seen
him in.

00:00:22.779 --> 00:00:23.779
​Braveheart

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:28.269
Flanagan is an extraordinarily Scottish man,
so it should come as no surprise that his

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:33.460
first big break was in 1995's Braveheart,
the epic historical drama directed by and

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:35.130
starring Mel Gibson.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.830
Flanagan played a villager named Morrison
whose wedding is interrupted by the repulsive

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:42.110
Lord Bottoms, who steals Morrison's bride
for the night.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.160
Happily, Morrison gets his revenge when he
joins WIlliam Wallace's army...

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:46.860
"It was my right!"

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:47.380
"Your right?

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.140
Well I'm here to claim the right of a husband!"

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.160
The Saint

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.190
This 1997 thriller cashed in on the then-solid
superstar status of Val Kilmer, who was coming

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.330
off his one-movie stint as Batman and still
sporting an action-hero's physique, perfect

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.990
for his role in The Saint.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:12.650
Kilmer plays the lead role, a smarmy thief-for-hire
with the world's most ridiculous collection

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.650
of disguises ...

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.730
"It's so early.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:18.350
You guys want to get some coffee or something?"

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:23.120
Of course, the billionaire Russian oligarch
who enlists the Saint also needs a couple

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.870
of loyal henchmen to help with his schemes
— enter Flanagan, who joined the cast as

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.240
a thug known as Scarface.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.860
For the most part, his role consists of hovering
nearby and looking intimidating.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.760
Flanagan was apparently not a fan of the movie's
leading man.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:43.090
In 2004, he "slowly and precisely" said this
into one journalist's tape recorder: "Val

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.090
Kilmer's a prick."

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.240
Face/Off

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.740
Not content to play just one role per year
as the right-hand man to a movie villain,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:56.580
in 1997 Flanagan also showed up in John Woo's
brilliant — and brilliantly absurd — Face/Off,

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:01.670
a film that was a giant hit at the box office,
despite its repulsive and ridiculous premise.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:06.520
Flanagan plays a Leo, a henchman to the evil
Castor Troy, a role played by both Nicolas

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.149
Cage and John Travolta...you know, because
of the face-swapping thing.

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:15.000
“I’d like to take his… his face… off.”

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.440
Flanagan turns up in multiple scenes as a
strong, silent member of the villain's support

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:28.879
staff, where he's easily identifiable as a
Bad Guy thanks to his stylishly sleazy turtleneck-and-blazer

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:29.879
combo.

00:02:29.879 --> 00:02:30.879
The Game

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:34.049
1997 was a big year for Flanagan.

00:02:34.049 --> 00:02:38.689
After playing a couple of toughs in The Saint
and Face/Off, he also had a memorable turn

00:02:38.689 --> 00:02:40.719
as a crazy cabbie in The Game.

00:02:40.719 --> 00:02:45.189
A twisted David Fincher thriller, Michael
Douglas starred as a cold-hearted businessman

00:02:45.189 --> 00:02:51.989
who ends up fighting for his life on his forty-eighth
birthday in an elaborate role-playing game...gone

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:52.989
mad!

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:57.230
Flanagan is on camera in this for only about
fifteen seconds, and has zero lines, but his

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.799
performance makes a big impression.

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:00.849
Gladiator

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:05.379
With one historical epic already under his
belt, Flanagan scored an even bigger part

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:11.329
in his next one in 2000: Ridley Scott's Gladiator,
where he played Maximus' loyal servant Cicero.

00:03:11.329 --> 00:03:15.480
It was one of the actor's most significant
cinematic roles yet, and really showed off

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.480
his range.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:20.499
Not only did Flanagan demonstrate that he
makes a totally convincing good guy, complete

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.870
with a noble and dramatic on screen death
...

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:25.920
"I'm sorry."

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.380
… but he also toned down his thick accent
considerably ...

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.860
"I do what I have to."

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.930
​Charlie's Angels: Full Throttle

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.139
Hollywood's always in need of a few good bad
guys.

00:03:38.139 --> 00:03:42.809
And by 2003, Flanagan was high on the list
of the industry's most eligible henchmen.

00:03:42.809 --> 00:03:43.809
"Lights!

00:03:43.809 --> 00:03:45.459
Somebody got the lights!"

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:51.129
His nameless roughhouser in ​Charlie's Angels:
Full Throttle, credited only as "Irish Henchman,"

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:55.499
was part of the squad assembled by the evil
Irishmen Seamus O'Grady.

00:03:55.499 --> 00:03:59.269
Flanagan took plenty of licks from the ladies,
but says Lucy Lui was the hardest-hitting

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:01.299
Angel in the trio.

00:04:01.299 --> 00:04:02.299
Sin City

00:04:02.299 --> 00:04:06.920
Flanagan next turned up in Robert Rodriguez's
gruesome 2005 film Sin City.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:12.209
There, he played a mercenary named Brian in
a vignette titled "The Big Fat Kill," where

00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:15.230
he memorably chucks a grenade at a mute assassin
...

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.320
"Suck on this, you stupid slag!"

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.610
… and then makes an elegant escape down
a manhole with Benicio del Toro's severed

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:29.110
head — surely a career highlight.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:30.759
When a Stranger Calls

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:36.310
This 2006 remake of the classic horror film
features Flanagan as the namesake stranger,

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:40.810
who terrorizes a hapless babysitter with a
series of threatening phone calls.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:44.590
Although Flanagan doesn't actually speak in
When a Stranger Calls — the creepy voice

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.800
on the line belongs to actor Lance Henriksen
from the Alien series — the image of him

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:53.060
in the back of a police car in the film's
final moments make it clear why he was a perfect

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.289
casting choice.

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:56.060
​Sons of Anarchy

00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:00.650
Flanagan's is best-known role is also the
one he played the longest, as fan favorite

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.540
"Chibs" Telford on the FX series Sons of Anarchy.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:07.319
"Jackie boy, this place is fantastic!"

00:05:07.319 --> 00:05:08.900
"I'm so excited."

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:13.650
The show tells the story of a gun-running
motorcycle gang that may or may not be loosely

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.900
based on the famous Hell's Angels.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:21.400
Flanagan played Telford for all seven seasons,
as he rose in the ranks to become Sergeant-at-Arms,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.669
Vice President, and finally President Motorcycle
Guy.

00:05:24.669 --> 00:05:26.860
Nice guys don't always finish last!

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.379
​There's more ...

00:05:28.379 --> 00:05:30.180
Still don't know where you've seen Flanagan?

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:35.259
Over the years, you may have spotted him on
one of several high-profile prime time properties,

00:05:35.259 --> 00:05:41.330
including Revenge, Gotham, and a memorable
turn as a loan shark on Law &amp; Order: SVU,

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.639
in which he actually has the gall to threaten
Ice-T ....

00:05:43.639 --> 00:05:46.930
"Tell your girlfriend she's gonna be sorry."

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:47.930
"Threatening a detective, huh?

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.800
Why don't we add that to the rest of your
charges?"

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.099
Going toe to toe with Ice T?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.580
That's pretty...cool.

00:05:58.129 --> 00:05:59.120
Thanks for watching!

00:05:59.129 --> 00:06:01.479
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:03.680
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

